# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-13: a full-screen page opened from a row of the listing goes back
# to the listing, not out to the adventuring screen (M5-E4d #305), and
# the second Escape is what gives the screen back.
# The listing after the page cannot be `equal` to the listing before it,
# because opening a row takes the `*` off it and the cursor's row
# changes; it is held still instead, which says it is a settled screen
# and not a page with a listing painted through it.
# A single leg, for not-log-giveback.leg's reason.

about a page from the listing goes back to the listing, and then out
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
cite-all
both code-wheel

# No document, and no gate: since #290 the possession proof is the act,
# so what a leg says is a condition rather than a digest, and the run is
# made on the boot the challenge never stops (#291, #293).
code-wheel-answered
seam journal
until 272156800
every 25

# A screen this seam draws is painted over successive arrivals, a few
# rows at a time, by the program's own drawing routines: about 230
# frames for a twenty-row page and about 130 for a ten-row listing,
# measured by hand (#305). A range starting sooner would measure the
# paint.
key L@7551
key A@7801
key N@9200
key Return@9800
key Escape@10800
key Escape@11800

rect bar 0,190,319,199

# The listing, the page, and the listing again: each settled.
same 9400-9775
same 10100-10775
same 11000-11775

equal 9200 12200 bar
